      "content": "That feeling of watching your life from the outside, like a spectator to your own fading performance, is incredibly isolating. If everything feels pointless, maybe the point isn't in finding a grand purpose, but in finding a very small, immediate relief. A single, quiet act—like the deliberate act of making a small, perfect cup of tea, or just focusing on the sensation of the air—can be a tiny anchor when the whole script feels meaningless.",
